39:Ta71,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Which sites can the car take me to?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The usual loop is Quba Mosque, Masjid al-Qiblatayn, the Seven Mosques (Al-Khandaq) area and Mount Uhud with its martyrs cemetery. You choose the stops and the order in the planner, and the driver waits at each one."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a Madinah Ziyarat trip take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A half-day is usually enough for the main sites, but the time depends on how long you stay at each stop and on prayer times and traffic. Tell us your pace and who is travelling and we plan the hours with you."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this a guided tour?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. This is a private transport service: the car and driver take you between the sites and wait. We do not provide a guide or religious guidance. For history and rulings use our Ziyarat sites guide or a qualified guide."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you pick us up from our hotel near Masjid an-Nabawi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Pickup is from the nearest permitted point to your hotel in the Central Area (Markaziyah) or from any other Madinah district. Access near the mosque is restricted, so give us the exact hotel name."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it suitable for elderly parents and children?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Tell us who is travelling and we suggest an SUV or van with easier boarding, plan longer waits and keep the car as close as allowed. We cannot guarantee access arrangements at the sites themselves, which the authorities control."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can we stop at Dhul Hulayfah (Abyar Ali) or visit Badr?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dhul Hulayfah is on the Makkah road, so ask for it on a Madinah to Makkah transfer. Badr is a separate half-day trip about 150 km from Madinah - see our Badr Ziyarat service. Whether to enter ihram at the Miqat is a religious question we cannot advise on."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is a Madinah Ziyarat car?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the vehicle and the hours. We do not publish a fixed list because it would not fit every plan: send your stops and passengers and we confirm one fixed fare on WhatsApp before booking, with no meter and no surge."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I cancel or change the plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Cancellation is free up to 24 hours before pickup, and you can change the stops, time or hotel on WhatsApp."}}]}25:[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$39"}}]]
